## 0.7 Project Detection

Identify the active project **from data**, not hardcoded names:

1. Read `.cuebert/workspace-manifest.json` — the `projects` object lists onboarded projects (may be empty early in M1).
2. `--project [name]` flag, REPO handoff, `@path` mentions, and open-file workspace paths resolve against those keys and `docs/projects/{name}/`.
3. If no project matches, set `Active Project` to `unknown` and use hub-level paths (`docs/projects/cuebert/`).

Do **not** assume legacy application repo names from other hubs.

## 0.8 Branch Awareness

Detect git branch of the active project. Record in Decision block. Check if branch matches any active plan slug.

